Heritage Selection Principle

Preservation requires selection.

The ecosystem generally favors preservation of ideas that demonstrate:

durability,
usefulness,
transferability,
explanatory power,
practical value,
historical significance,
developmental value,
or long-term relevance.

Preservation should be intentional rather than accidental.

